      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "flash_storage",
        "description": "W25Q128JV provides nonvolatile SPI NOR Flash storage for communication logging. It consumes VCC_3V3 and interfaces to the MCU over standard SPI: DI receives SPI_MOSI, DO drives SPI_MISO, CLK receives SPI_SCK, and CS is controlled by a dedicated flash chip-select from the MCU. The provided pin data also exposes WP and HOLD; because no separate controller resources for these functions are requested in the brief, their inactive operating policy must be established downstream so normal SPI logging remains available without assuming undocumented MCU connections. This device is a single SPI slave on the logging bus segment.",
        "id": "flash_storage"
